    "created_at": "2018-11-26T14:59:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-26T14:59:34Z",
    "body": "> Using \"unit of related similar-origin browsing contexts\" never made much sense as a browsing context could always hold several cross-site documents.\r\n\r\nI don't understand this. If a browsing context held a cross-site document, it would no longer be in that UORSOBCs.\r\n\r\nIn general I disagree that agents are more primitive or useful than UORSOBCs, but we can discuss that over in the HTML issue I guess.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
